From c23b076530132a59a0a29ecbffaa39c8166cfb03 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <81541646+RyanTheTide@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 08:52:14 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 56/57] wayland/session-lock: Keep captures from showing what
 is behind the lock

The lock is painted above everything on the stage, but some ways of
getting at the screen contents went around it:

- Window screen casts (PipeWire window streams) and
  meta_window_actor_paint_to_content()/_paint_to_bitmap() paint the
  window actor on its own, so a window cast started before the lock
  kept streaming the window, and a window screenshot showed it.
  While locked they now get transparent images of the window's size,
  damage of the window is not announced to its streams, and on lock
  and unlock every streamed window records a frame right away (blank,
  then the window again).
- wlr-screencopy captures held only the lock, but copy_with_damage
  reported the damage of the windows painted behind it, which tells a
  recording client when and where a hidden window changes. While
  locked the stage damage is ignored; locking, unlocking and commits
  of lock surfaces and their subsurfaces damage the whole output.
- The foreign toplevel list is frozen while locked.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
